


MKLOST+FOUND(8)     UNIX Programmer's Manual	  MKLOST+FOUND(8)



NNAAMMEE
     mklost - make a lost+found directory for fsck

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     //eettcc//mmkklloosstt

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     A directory _l_o_s_t+_f_o_u_n_d is created in the current directory
     and a number of empty files are created therein and then
     removed so that there will be empty slots for _f_s_c_k(8).  This
     command should be used whenever a new file system is created
     with _m_k_f_s(8) or _n_e_w_f_s(8).

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     fsck(8), mkfs(8)








































